tr_by=hand
why=pelt#49, ruling #113: with set -o autocd an interactive shell runs a command whose name has a slash and names a directory (relative, absolute with a trailing slash, .., ~ after expansion) as cd -- NAME: status 0, PWD and OLDPWD as cd sets them, cd - goes back; nothing said. bash 5.3 with shopt -s autocd answers the same and also writes cd -- NAME on standard error; zsh 5.9 with AUTO_CD the same, silent (black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base/bash-i-autocd/p01-slash, zsh-i-autocd/p01-slash); dash has no such option. Written by hand from pelt trunk's answers to the explicit cd -- NAME session (notes/sh23-evidence/handtr.py)
